{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1486133-questions-about-trinity-continuum-aberrant-character-creation","id":1486133,"title":"Questions about Trinity Continuum Aberrant Character Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-09T18:19:17-07:00","id":1486133,"title":"Questions about Trinity Continuum Aberrant Character Creation","content":"My players and I are preparing for our first storypath game. We are going to play Aberrant and have started making characters. We've started by making the baseline version of their characters. We haven't reached the point where we add the Nova template yet. My players had path concepts that didn't match up to existing paths in the rulebook so we are creating new paths. I want to make sure that I'm not steering them wrong and have some questions. Any clarifications would be much appreciated.<br /> <br /> Question #1: Can there be skill redundancies across paths? For example, can an origin path and a role path share one or more skills if they fit with the path concept, or must each path have different skills? <br /> <br /> Question #2: Page 37 of the core rulebook, explains that my players gain 2 dots for Edges per path. On page 41 in the section on path creation, I'm confused by the following sentences, &quot;When creating the Path, a player chooses 15 points worth of Edges using each edge's maximum number of dots.&quot; Is this referring to buying the list of Edges that can then have dots distributed as described on p. 37?<br /> <br /> Question #3: Are Paths and Edges from Aberrant allowed when creating my player's baseline characters or are they only allowed after the nova template has been applied? It seems like Paths would make sense but Edges like Attunement and Dormancy seem like they would only make sense after the character is a nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25223-phdoom","name":"PhDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T19:18:10-07:00","id":1486135,"title":"","content":"1) Yes, there\u2019s nothing stopping each Path covering the same skills. <br /> <br /> 2) Each Path has 15 dots of Edges available. However, the player only gets to pick 2 dots worth from those Edges when choosing the Path.<br /> <br /> 3) This depends on what works for your game. While you\u2019re right that things like Attunement and Dormancy don\u2019t make much sense for baselines, most groups just roll with it and don\u2019t sweat that level of detail too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T19:21:49-07:00","id":1486136,"title":"","content":"Thank you again for the quick and very helpful clarifications Bunyip!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25223-phdoom","name":"PhDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T19:23:26-07:00","id":1486137,"title":"","content":"#1 - Yes, you can have the same Skill as part of multiple Paths.<br /> <br /> #2 - Each Path should have 15 dots worth of appropriate Edges associated with it. This way, if you wind up eventually taking the max 5 levels in the Path, you'll have 10 dots in Edges, leaving you some leeway in case you took any of the Edges as part of another Path.<br /> <br /> #3 - They are allowed. A lot of the Storypath games are like that. Psiads have the Psiad Origin Path, even though most Psiads don't develop their powers until their teens or twenties.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way; NPCs aren't normally built with three Paths, they have whatever qualities suit them. PCs get three Paths, but nothing says they developed all those Paths prior to becoming Inspired. After all, if you're running a Teragen campaign, how are you expected to join the Teragen Allegiance before erupting as a nova? Whatever power related Edges they have and whatever Allegiance they've joined, they're things that have happened since they erupted.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you could argue that some of your character's Attribute dots developed after they gained their powers. Maybe they only had three dots in each of the Physical, Mental, and Social Arenas, and erupting suddenly boosted their Social and Physical Arenas to five and seven dots. This way, your former couch potato suddenly has a body like a pro weight lifter. That's perfectly fine as long as the point totals all add up in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}